course: dictionary
lesson: 10540
title: The ultimate word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ultimate can mean final, the very end of a long process. It can also mean the best, greatest or most extreme of its kind. Use the words around it to choose. «Hinduism has many gods and goddesses, and many Hindus see them as forms of one ultimate reality.» The clue is «one»: the ultimate reality is the most basic truth behind everything.
explain: Advertisers love this word. «The ultimate pizza» does not mean the last pizza in the shop; it means the best pizza you could imagine. «The ultimate challenge» means the hardest challenge there is. Ask yourself: is the writer praising something as the best, or describing the very last step?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «the final pizza» and «the best pizza» instead of «the ultimate pizza». The best swap is the one that still makes sense. Ultimate is often close to final, but it can also mean best, so the context decides.
fact: Ultimate means final, the very last stage of a long process.
fact: Ultimate also means the best, greatest or most extreme of its kind.
fact: Ultimate can mean basic or most important, as in «the ultimate cause».
fact: «The ultimate in comfort» is an informal phrase meaning the very best example of comfort.
fact: Ultimate frisbee is a team game played with a flying disc.
exercise: «The ultimate pizza» in an advert means what? | The pizza that arrives last | The best pizza | *The best pizza you could imagine | The cheapest pizza in town
exercise: Mia says the ultimate goal in a story is the first thing that happens. What does ultimate goal mean? | *The final aim the hero is working towards | A small pet the hero owns | The first thing that happens in the story | A game with a flying disc
exercise: Which description matches ultimate frisbee? | A dance with ribbons | A running race around a track | *A team game played with a flying disc | A card game for two players
exercise: Which description matches ultimate frisbee? | A card game for two players | A running race around a track | A dance with ribbons | *A team game played with a flying disc
test: In «the ultimate in comfort», what does the ultimate in mean? | A small chair | *The very best example of comfort | A cold kind of comfort | The start of comfort
test: «The ultimate cause of the flood was the heavy rain.» What does ultimate mean here? | *Basic or most important | Very small | Wet and muddy | Happening first
exam: Which sentence uses ultimate to mean the very end? | We ate the ultimate sandwich at lunch | Our ultimate dog is brown | He wore an ultimate hat | *The ultimate prize was given after the last round
